item.description:
This section contains resources related to _filters_.

Advanced searches must specify a set of filters (more on filters 
can be found under [Resources](#resources)). A _simple filter_ is defined by three fields, 
two of which are mandatory and the third one depends on the operator. 

| Field| Description| Mandatory | Type |
|    ---   |   --- | ---  |---  |
| key      | **label** of the field    | YES | string |
| operator | operation to be performed | YES | string |
| value    | value of the operation    |     | String/Array/Object |

In order to be able to build such filters, fields and available operators for each field must be known and thats the 
point of all resources listed in this section.

## Standard filter operators

Common operators are shown in the table below, some operations are not allowed for every filter.

A complete list of available fields and allowed operations can be obtained by requesting a GET on
its own filters/_resource_ section.

Note: _Item_ used in the table below can refer to an attribute, property, field, etc.

| Operator | Arity | Type | Description |
| --- | :---: | ---  | --- |
| exists   | Unary | -  | Existence check. <br /> True when the item has its value defined  |
| !exists  | Unary | -   |  Non-existence check. <br /> True when the item has its value undefined |
| eq       | Binary   | value | Equality check.<br /> True if the item has the same value as the one provided <br /> When applied to a text value, the comparison ignores case  |
| !eq      | Binary  | value | Inequality check.<br /> False if the item has the same value as the one provided  <br /> When applied to a text value, the comparison is ignoring case |
| like     | Binary  | value | Contains check. <br /> Check if supplied string is contained within value  |
|  in      | Binary  | list | Match check. <br /> Determines if the value matches any of the values specified in the list<br /> __Note__: Multiselect  and Dropdown attributes are case sensitive |
|  !in     | Binary  | list | Do not match check. <br /> Determines if the value doesn't match any of the values specified in the list<br /> __Note__: Multiselect  and Dropdown attributes are case sensitive   |
|  gt      | Binary  | value | Greater than. <br /> True if items' value is greater than provided  |
|  gte     | Binary  | value | Greater or equal than. <br /> True if items' value is greater or equal than provided     |
|  lt      | Binary  | value | Greater than. <br /> True if items' value is greater than provided |
|  lte     | Binary  | value | Less or equal than. <br /> True if items' value is greater than provided |
|  text_search | Binary | value | Text search <br /> Allows the user to search for text in several items <br /> Item list must be provided as "field" value <br />  |

## Response structure
Suscessful responses from filter endpoints are always wrapped in a result _data_ object :

* data: List of items returned from the API:
   * attributes: List of attributes _objects_.
   * properties: List of meta properties _objects_

Both _attributes_ and _properties_  _objects_ share structure, which is compound of:
* key: key of the field, this is what must be used in "field" 
* operators: List of available operators for this field 
* options: Optional, list allowed values for fields with a limited subset or values 
* filter_type: Type of the filter, mainly informative

You can find some response examples in each endpoint


## Filter operator examples
This section shows a small example of each operator.


* `[exists]` Get items whose thumbnail is defined 
    ```json
    {"filters": [
                [ {"field":"thumbnail","operator":"exists"} ] 
              ]}
    ```

* `[!exists]` Get items whose thumbnail is not defined 
    ```json
    {"filters": [       
                [ {"field":"thumbnail","operator":"!exists"} ]
              ]}
    ```

* `[eq]` Get items whose sku __is__ _Sample - 001_ 
    ```json
    {"filters": [ 
                [ 
                    {"field":"sku","operator":"eq", "value":"Sample - 001"}
                ]
              ]}
    ```

* `[!eq]` Get items whose stock is not equal to 123
    ```json
    {"filters": [ 
                [ 
                    {"field":"attributes.stock","operator":"!eq", "value":123}
                ]
              ]}
    ```

* `[like]` Get items whose name contains "sample" in any position
    ```json
    {"filters": [ 
                [ 
                    {"field":"attributes.name","operator":"like", "value":"sample"}
                ]
              ]}
    ```

* `[in]` Get items belonging to, at least, one of the specified categories 
    ```json
    {"filters": [ 
                [ 
                    {"field":"categories", "operator":"in", "value":["5c4ed7f62f0985001c233277","5c4ed7f62f0985001c233278","5c4ed7f62f0985001c233279"]}  
                ]
              ]}
    ```

* `[!in]` Get items not having, at least, one of the specified values 
    ```json
    {"filters": [ 
                [ 
                    {"field": "attributes.multiselect", "operator": "!in", "value": ["option 1", "option 3"]}
                ]
              ]}
    ```

* `[gt]` Get items whose price is greater than 120
    ```json
    {"filters": [ 
                [ 
                    {"field": "attributes.price", "operator": "gt", "value": 120}
                ]
              ]}
    ```

* `[gte]` Get items whose price is greater than or equal to 120  
    ```json
    {"filters": [ 
                [ 
                    {"field": "price", "operator": "gte", "value": 120}
                ]
              ]}
    ```

* `[lt]` Get items whose price is less than 120
    ```json
    {"filters": [ 
                [ 
                    {"field": "attributes.price", "operator": "lt", "value": 120}
                ]
              ]}
    ```

* `[lte]` Get items whose price is less than or equal to 120  
    ```json
    {"filters": [ 
                [ 
                    {"field": "attributes.price", "operator": "lte", "value": 120}    
                ]
              ]}
    ```

* Get items whose price is greater than or equal to 100 **AND** less than 120  
    We need a _compound_ filter with an AND condition so:
    ```json
    {"filters": [ 
                [ 
                    {"field": "attributes.price", "operator": "gte", "value": 100 },
                    {"field": "attributes.price", "operator": "lt", "value": 120}
                ]
              ]}
    ```

* Get items whose 
    a) price is greater than or equal to 100 **AND** less than 120
    **OR**  b)   sku __is__ _Sample - 001_ 
    ```json
    {"filters": [ 
                [ 
                    {"field": "price", "operator": "gte", "value": 100 },
                    {"field": "price", "operator": "lt", "value": 120}
                ],
                [
                    {"field":"sku","operator":"eq", "value":"Sample - 001"}
                ]
              ]}
    ```

* `[text_search]` Get items containing 'kettle' in any of 'sku' or 'label' fields
    ```json
    {"filters": [
                 [
                    {"field":["sku","label"],"operator":"text_search","value":"kettle"}     
                  ]
              ]}
    ```

